# 3. OWASP TOP 10:2025 REVISION

| # | Category | Core Idea |
|---|---|---|
| A01 | Broken Access Control | User can perform actions they should not be allowed to perform |
| A02 | Security Misconfiguration | Unsafe configuration/defaults |
| A03 | Software Supply Chain Failures | Risks in dependencies/build/update supply chain |
| A04 | Cryptographic Failures | Weak/missing protection of sensitive data |
| A05 | Injection | Untrusted input changes interpreter behavior |
| A06 | Insecure Design | Security weakness in architecture/design |
| A07 | Authentication Failures | Weak or broken identity/session controls |
| A08 | Software or Data Integrity Failures | Untrusted or tampered software/data |
| A09 | Security Logging & Alerting Failures | Important security events aren't adequately logged/alerted |
| A10 | Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions | Unsafe handling of errors/failures/unexpected states |

### Memory

> **ACCESS → CONFIG → SUPPLY → CRYPTO → INJECT → DESIGN → AUTH → INTEGRITY → LOG → EXCEPTION**

