# 4. THE MOST IMPORTANT VULNERABILITIES

## SQL Injection

```text
Untrusted input
      ↓
SQL query
      ↓
Query behavior altered
```

### Primary defense

> **Parameterized queries / prepared statements**

---

## XSS

```text
Untrusted input
      ↓
Web application
      ↓
Browser
      ↓
Unexpected script execution
```

### Primary defense

> **Context-appropriate output encoding**

---

## Directory Traversal

```text
User-controlled path
       ↓
Path processing
       ↓
Unintended filesystem location
```

### Primary defense

> **Controlled identifiers + canonicalization + allowlisting + least privilege**

---

## CSRF

```text
Victim logged in
       ↓
Attacker-controlled cross-site request
       ↓
Victim browser
       ↓
Authenticated state-changing request
```

### Primary defenses

> **CSRF tokens + appropriate SameSite policy + origin validation + safe HTTP method design**

