# 5. SQLi VS XSS VS CSRF VS TRAVERSAL

| Vulnerability | Main Target | Main Problem |
|---|---|---|
| SQLi | Database/interpreter | Input changes SQL behavior |
| XSS | Browser | Untrusted content executes in browser |
| CSRF | Application action | Victim browser sends unwanted authenticated request |
| Directory Traversal | Filesystem | User-controlled path escapes intended location |

### Memory

```text
SQLi        → DATABASE
XSS         → BROWSER
CSRF        → REQUEST
Traversal   → FILESYSTEM
```

