# 11. XSS REVISION

## Definition

> XSS occurs when untrusted content is improperly handled and interpreted as executable content in a user's browser.

### Three major types

```text
Reflected
Stored
DOM-based
```

### Memory

> **R-S-D**

**Reflected → Stored → DOM**

---

# 12. XSS LOCATIONS

Potential inputs:

```text
Search
Comments
Profile fields
Reviews
Chat
URL parameters
Error messages
Rich text
API responses
```

---

# 13. XSS DEFENSE

Primary general defense:

> **Context-appropriate output encoding**

Additional defenses:

```text
CSP
Safe DOM APIs
Secure framework practices
Input validation
HttpOnly cookies
Secure cookie configuration
```

