# 15. DIRECTORY TRAVERSAL REVISION

## Definition

> Directory Traversal is a vulnerability in which improperly handled user-controlled path information allows access outside the intended directory.

Common parameters:

```text
file=
filename=
path=
document=
download=
template=
page=
image=
resource=
```

---

# 16. TRAVERSAL DEFENSE

### Best approach

Instead of accepting arbitrary filesystem paths:

```text
User
 ↓
File ID
 ↓
Server-side lookup
 ↓
Known file
```

Also use:

```text
Canonicalization
+
Allowlisting
+
Least privilege
+
Safe archive extraction
```

---

# 17. ZIP SLIP

Zip Slip is a related path traversal problem involving archive extraction.

Unsafe concept:

```text
Archive
 ↓
Malicious path
 ↓
Extraction
 ↓
File escapes extraction directory
```

Safe extraction must ensure each resolved destination remains inside the intended extraction directory.

