# ⭐ DAY 28 ONE-LINE EXAM ANSWER

> **Web application security testing involves systematically mapping an authorized application, identifying attack surfaces and inputs, testing authentication, authorization, input handling, sessions and configuration, validating potential vulnerabilities such as SQL Injection, XSS, Directory Traversal and CSRF, assessing their impact, reporting findings, applying remediation and retesting.**

